From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hibreak <hibreak@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:27:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] e-ink: fixes from an audit: sleep signal, fingerprint, sleep
 screen, users

- vendor.xrz.hibreak_sleep has one writer, the power manager's Notifier.
  PhoneWindowManager's write came from a queue: after a quick sleep and wake
  its late "asleep" followed the Notifier's "awake" (a bogus sleep hold).
- vendor.xrz.hibreak_finger goes back to 0 with the unlock and going to sleep:
  a match that unlocked nothing no longer holds the next wake-up.
- Sleep screen: one line HH:MM in landscape (two lines pushed the date and
  icons off the screen); no icons of lock-screen-secret notifications; icons
  that fail to load are not loaded again on every change.
- Display off between updates: DOZE <-> DOZE_SUSPEND while the display is on
  no longer restarts off_ms; off_ms < 0 keeps the display on after a tick.
- No-animations option: the scale reset is posted, not set from inside the
  listener (Compose ended with the window manager's scale).
- Wallpaper colours for the clock, icons and keyguard status bar of the
  current user, not SystemUI's own (secondary users); the sleep screen's
  weather from the system user, where HiBreakParts writes it.
- Touch boost: LAUNCH counts as sent only when the HAL took it.
- Window outline skipped for windows thinner than the line; brightness slider
  outline radius on the line's centre; keyguard scrim alpha "NaN" rejected;
  weather icon cache bounded.
